{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b4451223-7296-5ed3-b057-d155006ac139",
    "description": "Runs the Trustee platform API end to end without writing code.\n\n**Demo-only keys.** Request bodies are signed in advance with Ed25519 keys derived from seeds that are published in `scripts/make_postman.py`. These keys exist only to sign these samples. Do not register them on a server that holds money, and do not reuse them as real identities.\n\n**Run it.** Start the API (`uvicorn trustee.arena.api:app --port 8000`) and run the collection. Folder 2 is the honest path: the deal settles and PayPal captures the held funds (dry-run when no PayPal credentials are set). Folder 3 proves three refusals: a forged signature, a price over the mandate cap, and a delivery signed by the wrong party. Folder 4 runs the same deal over the A2A JSON-RPC binding (`POST /a2a`): it needs the identities from folder 2, so run the folders in order.\n\n**Re-running.** A fresh server gives a clean pass. On the same server, registrations return 200, the identical mandates and deal return 201 and 200, the delivery returns 409 (the deal has already settled) and the attestation returns 200 as a no-op.\n\nThe API contract is `openapi/trustee-v1.json`. The SDK workflow is documented in `docs/SDKS.md`.",
    "name": "Trustee Platform API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
